+---
+id: task-001-implement-json-pointer-rfc-6901-resolvepointer
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) resolvePointer"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Context
+
+First feature of `json-toolkit`: a shared way for services to refer to a value inside a JSON
+document, per RFC 6901 (JSON Pointer). Later features (e.g. JSON Patch) will build on it.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, along with the
+  `JsonValue` type used for its signature.
+- Behaviour follows RFC 6901 sections 3-5: empty pointer resolves to the whole document; tokens
+  are split on `/` and unescaped (`~1` → `/`, then `~0` → `~`); object members are looked up with
+  `hasOwnProperty` (no prototype lookups); array tokens must match `0` or `[1-9][0-9]*` (no
+  leading zeros, no `-` append token) and must be in bounds.
+- Throws a plain `Error` both when the pointer string is syntactically invalid (missing leading
+  `/`, malformed `~` escape) and when it does not resolve to a value (missing member, index out
+  of bounds, `-` token, traversal through a scalar).
+- Tests (`src/index.test.ts`, run via `node --test`, 9 cases): written first and confirmed red
+  (module did not exist) before implementing, per the testing directive. Covers the whole RFC 6901
+  section 5 worked example (happy path) plus one error-path test per failure mode listed above.
+  All new behaviour, so classified red-first.
+- Documented the feature in `README.md` with a usage example.
+- Verified `src/index.ts` compiles cleanly under the project's strict `tsconfig.json` using a
+  temporary, uncommitted `typescript` install (not added as a dependency).
+
+## Follow-up (recorded as a decision-log, not resolved here)
+
+Typechecking `src/index.test.ts` itself fails today (`node:test` types unresolved without
+`@types/node`; the `./index.ts` import specifier needed for `node --test` to run TypeScript
+source directly is rejected by `tsc` without `allowImportingTsExtensions`, which this project's
+build-oriented `tsconfig.json` cannot enable without restructuring the build). No typecheck
+script exists in `package.json` yet, so this does not regress anything currently enforced, but it
+is a pre-existing tooling gap worth a deliberate decision rather than an incidental fix.
